# Testing Standards

## Test Structure

### File Naming
- Unit tests: `{filename}.test.{ext}`
- Integration tests: `{filename}.integration.test.{ext}`
- E2E tests: `{feature}.e2e.test.{ext}`

### Test Organization
```
describe('[ModuleName]', () => {
  describe('[functionName]', () => {
    it('should [expected behavior] when [condition]', () => {
      // Arrange
      // Act
      // Assert
    });
  });
});
```

## Coverage Requirements
- New functions: Minimum 80% coverage
- Critical paths: 100% coverage
- Error handling: All error branches tested

## Test Independence
- No test should depend on another test's state
- Use fresh fixtures for each test
- Clean up created resources in afterEach

## Mocking Rules
- Mock external services and APIs
- Do not mock the module under test
- Prefer dependency injection over module mocking

## Forbidden
- `.skip` or `.only` in committed tests
- Hardcoded test data that duplicates production data
- Tests without assertions
- Sleep/delay in tests (use waitFor patterns)
